

## Efficient High-Order Masked Batch Dilithium
This repository contains a high‑performance implementation of Dilithium with masking countermeasures at arbitrary security orders, supporting batch signature generation for improved throughput.

To replicate the benchmark results for different masking orders and batch sizes, the macros `MASKING_ORDER` and `BATCH_SIZE` need to be set in the file `masking_interface.h`.  
In `masking_interface.h`, one will find a macro to choose the security order (`MASKING_ORDER`) and a macro to define the batch size for batch signing (`BATCH_SIZE`).  
After setting the desired parameters:

```bash

cd Dilithium
make simple_tests
./main
```

Note that in order to avoid editing the code multiple times when iterating over different orders and batch sizes, an automated Python script called `run_benchmark.py` can compile and execute the benchmarks for multiple configurations automatically.  
The tests have been performed primarily for the Dilithium‑2 parameter set.


